{"task_id": "HumanEval/12", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\n\ndef longest(strings: List[str]) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"Out of list of strings, return the longest one. Return the first one in case of multiple\n    strings of the same length. Return None if the input list is empty.\"\"\"\n\n    # Handle FR4: Return None if the input list is empty.\n    if not strings:\n        return None\n\n    # Initialize variables for tracking the longest string and its length.\n    longest_str: Optional[str] = None\n    max_length = -1\n\n    # Iterate through the list to find the longest string.\n    for current_string in strings:\n        current_string_length = len(current_string)\n        # Handle FR2: Update if a longer string is found.\n        # Handle FR3: If lengths are equal, the first encountered is kept by not updating.\n        if current_string_length > max_length:\n            longest_str = current_string\n            max_length = current_string_length\n\n    # Handle FR5: Return the determined longest string.\n    return longest_str\n```"}
