{"task_id": "HumanEval/12", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\n\ndef longest(strings: List[str]) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"Finds the longest string from a list, returning the first occurrence in case of ties.\n    Returns None if the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not strings:\n        return None\n\n    longest_so_far = strings[0]\n    max_length = len(strings[0])\n\n    for current_string in strings[1:]:\n        current_length = len(current_string)\n        if current_length > max_length:\n            longest_so_far = current_string\n            max_length = current_length\n\n    return longest_so_far\n```"}
