{"task_id": "HumanEval/24", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\" For a given number n, find the largest number that divides n evenly, smaller than n.\n    The function iterates downwards from n-1 to find the first divisor.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    for d in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        if n % d == 0:\n            return d\n    # This line is technically unreachable for n > 1 as 1 is always a divisor.\n    # It serves as a safeguard and covers prime numbers where the loop reaches d=1.\n    return 1\n```"}
