{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_third(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Sorts elements at indices divisible by three in a list, preserving others.\n    Returns a new list with sorted third-indexed elements and original non-third-indexed elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    output_list = list(l)\n    divisible_elements_values = []\n    divisible_elements_indices = []\n\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            divisible_elements_values.append(l[i])\n            divisible_elements_indices.append(i)\n\n    divisible_elements_values.sort()\n\n    for j in range(len(divisible_elements_indices)):\n        original_index = divisible_elements_indices[j]\n        sorted_value = divisible_elements_values[j]\n        output_list[original_index] = sorted_value\n\n    return output_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_third(l: list):\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the indicies that are not divisible by three, while its values at the indicies that are divisible by three are equal\n    to the values of the corresponding indicies of l, but sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n    l_prime = list(l)  # Create a shallow copy of the input list.\n    divisible_elements = []\n\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            divisible_elements.append(l[i])\n\n    divisible_elements.sort()\n\n    sorted_idx = 0\n    for i in range(len(l_prime)):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            l_prime[i] = divisible_elements[sorted_idx]\n            sorted_idx += 1\n\n    return l_prime\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/32", "solution": "import math\n\n\ndef poly(xs: list, x: float):\n    \"\"\"Evaluates polynomial with coefficients xs at point x.\"\"\"\n    return sum([coeff * math.pow(x, i) for i, coeff in enumerate(xs)])\n\n\ndef find_zero(xs: list):\n    \"\"\"Finds a zero point for polynomial with coefficients xs.\"\"\"\n    # Assumes input adheres to problem constraints: even length coefficients (odd degree),\n    # and a non-zero largest coefficient, which guarantees at least one real root.\n\n    low = -100.0  # Lower bound of the search range\n    high = 100.0  # Upper bound of the search range\n    tolerance = 1e-6\n    max_iterations = 1000\n\n    f_low = poly(xs, low)\n    f_high = poly(xs, high)\n\n    # Return if an endpoint is already a root (within tolerance)\n    if abs(f_low) < tolerance:\n        return low\n    if abs(f_high) < tolerance:\n        return high\n\n    for _ in range(max_iterations):\n        mid = (low + high) / 2\n        f_mid = poly(xs, mid)\n\n        if abs(f_mid) < tolerance:\n            return mid\n\n        # Narrow the search interval based on the sign of the function values\n        if f_low * f_mid < 0:\n            high = mid\n            f_high = f_mid\n        else:\n            low = mid\n            f_low = f_mid\n\n    # Return the midpoint as the best approximation after maximum iterations\n    return (low + high) / 2```"}
