{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\ndef fib4(n: int):\\\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    This function computes the n-th element of the Fib4 number sequence efficiently without recursion.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n    else:\n        # Initialize the last four Fib4 numbers: fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n        # These represent fib4(i-4), fib4(i-3), fib4(i-2), fib4(i-1) respectively in the loop\n        a, b, c, d = 0, 0, 2, 0\n\n        for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n            next_fib = a + b + c + d\n            a = b\n            b = c\n            c = d\n            d = next_fib\n        return d\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "```python\ndef median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # For an odd number of elements, the median is the middle element.\n        return sorted_l[n // 2]\n    else:\n        # For an even number, the median is the average of the two middle elements.\n        mid1 = sorted_l[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_l[n // 2]\n        return (mid1 + mid2) / 2.0\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "def modp(n: int, p: int):\n    \"\"\"Return 2^n modulo p using binary exponentiation for efficiency.\n    This method correctly handles large inputs by applying the modulo at each step.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = 1\n    base = 2\n\n    while n > 0:\n        if n % 2 == 1:\n            result = (result * base) % p\n        base = (base * base) % p\n        n //= 2\n\n    return result"}
