{"task_id": "HumanEval/57", "solution": "```python\ndef _is_non_decreasing(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a list is non-strictly increasing (each element >= previous).\n    Returns True if the list is non-decreasing, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    for i in range(len(l) - 1):\n        if l[i] > l[i + 1]:\n            return False\n    return True\n\ndef _is_non_increasing(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a list is non-strictly decreasing (each element <= previous).\n    Returns True if the list is non-increasing, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    for i in range(len(l) - 1):\n        if l[i] < l[i + 1]:\n            return False\n    return True\n\ndef monotonic(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a list is monotonically increasing or decreasing.\n    Returns True if the list is monotonic (increasing, decreasing, or constant), False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(l) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    return _is_non_decreasing(l) or _is_non_increasing(l)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/57", "solution": "```python\ndef _is_increasing(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the list is monotonically increasing.\n    Returns True if each element is greater than or equal to the previous one.\"\"\"\n    for i in range(1, len(l)):\n        if l[i] < l[i-1]:\n            return False\n    return True\n\ndef _is_decreasing(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the list is monotonically decreasing.\n    Returns True if each element is less than or equal to the previous one.\"\"\"\n    for i in range(1, len(l)):\n        if l[i] > l[i-1]:\n            return False\n    return True\n\ndef monotonic(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True is list elements are monotonically increasing or decreasing.\n    Special consideration is given to empty lists and single-element lists, which are considered monotonic.\n    >>> monotonic([1, 2, 4, 20])\n    True\n    >>> monotonic([1, 20, 4, 10])\n    False\n    >>> monotonic([4, 1, 0, -10])\n    True\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(l) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    return _is_increasing(l) or _is_decreasing(l)\n```\n"}
