{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "```python\ndef circular_shift(x: int, shift: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Circular shifts digits of x right by shift, returning as a string.\n    If shift exceeds number of digits, returns digits reversed.\n    \"\"\"\n    string_x = str(x)\n    n = len(string_x)\n\n    if shift > n:\n        # FR6: Return digits reversed if shift is strictly greater than n.\n        return string_x[::-1]\n    else:\n        # FR7: Calculate effective_shift as shift % n.\n        effective_shift = shift % n\n        # FR8: Perform a right circular shift.\n        return string_x[-effective_shift:] + string_x[:-effective_shift]\n```"}
