{"task_id": "HumanEval/100", "solution": "```python\ndef make_a_pile(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer n, you have to make a pile of n levels of stones.\n    The first level has n stones.\n    The number of stones in the next level is:\n        - the next odd number if n is odd.\n        - the next even number if n is even.\n    Return the number of stones in each level in a list, where element at index\n    i represents the number of stones in the level (i+1).\n\n    Examples:\n    >>> make_a_pile(3)\n    [3, 5, 7]\n    \"\"\"\n    pile = []\n    current_stones = n\n    pile.append(current_stones)\n\n    for _ in range(n - 1):\n        current_stones += 2\n        pile.append(current_stones)\n\n    return pile\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "```python\ndef closest_integer(value):\n    '''\n    Create a function that takes a value (string) representing a number\n    and returns the closest integer to it. If the number is equidistant\n    from two integers, round it away from zero.\n    '''\n    numerical_value = float(value)\n    abs_numerical_value = abs(numerical_value)\n    floor_int = int(abs_numerical_value)\n    fractional_part = abs_numerical_value - floor_int\n\n    if fractional_part >= 0.5:\n        # Round up for absolute value (away from zero for .5, or standard round up)\n        rounded_abs_value = floor_int + 1\n    else:\n        # Round down for absolute value\n        rounded_abs_value = floor_int\n\n    if numerical_value >= 0:\n        return rounded_abs_value\n    else:\n        return -rounded_abs_value\n```"}
